  "flow_summary": "The system performed well in managing a difficult, disorganized patient, consistently using redirection and breaking down complex questions to ensure clarity. However, the system struggled with the standardized questionnaires (PHQ-9 and GAD-7), frequently repeating questions due to the patient's confusion rather than efficiently guiding them through the scale, which led to a repetitive and somewhat mechanical interaction during those sections.",
  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "category": "questionnaire_management",
      "evidence": "The system repeatedly re-asked PHQ-9 and GAD-7 items when the patient expressed confusion, rather than providing a more concise or supportive way to keep the patient on track. For example: 'PHQ-9 Question 1: Over the last two weeks, how often have you been bothered by little interest or pleasure in doing things?' was asked three times."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "flow",
      "evidence": "In the GAD-7 section, the system asked 'GAD-7 Question 2: Over the last two weeks, how often have you had difficulty stopping or controlling worrying?' three times before receiving a valid answer."
    }
  ],
